// `m$+ [i, 0, 0]`: a row written as a literal, appended «N» times. Appending
// does not depend on how many rows there already are, so the whole is linear;
// an engine that copies the receiver because the operand is a literal is
// quadratic.
m = []
@ i:1..«N» { m$+ [i, 0, 0] }
>> m$# + m[«N»>1] ¶
